{"id":"60e0273340500623bea7301b1f9af39ac2b002de","url":"https://zigbyexample.neocities.org/","title":"Zig by Example","site_name":"Info Flow","source":"Lobsters (技术社区)","byline":null,"excerpt":"Zig is a general-purpose programming language and toolchain for maintaining robust, optimal and reusable software. Please read the official documentation to learn more.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div>\n\n\n\n<p>\n<a href=\"https://ziglang.org/\">Zig</a> is a general-purpose programming language and toolchain for maintaining robust, optimal and reusable software. Please read the <a href=\"https://ziglang.org/documentation/0.16.0/\">official documentation</a> to learn more.\n</p>\n\n<p>\n<i>Zig by Example</i> is a hands-on introduction to Zig using annotated example programs.\n</p>\n\n<p>\n<strong>The examples are written for version 0.16.</strong> Check which version you’re using if something isn’t working.\n</p>\n\n\n<h2>Getting Started</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"hello-world.html\">Hello, World!</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"formatted-output.html\">Formatted Output</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"unit-tests.html\">Unit Tests</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"basic-types.html\">Basic Types</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"variables.html\">Variables</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"illegal-behavior.html\">Illegal Behavior</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"build-modes.html\">Build Modes</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Basic Types</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"integers.html\">Integers</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"integer-operators.html\">Integer Operators</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"floating-point-numbers.html\">Floating-point Numbers</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Functions and Errors</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"functions.html\">Functions</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"errors.html\">Errors</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"assertions.html\">Assertions</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Control Flow</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"if-statements.html\">If Statements</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"switch-statements.html\">Switch Statements</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"while-loops.html\">While Loops</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"for-loops.html\">For Loops</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"blocks.html\">Blocks</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"defer.html\">Defer</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"errdefer.html\">Errdefer</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Compound Types</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"arrays.html\">Arrays</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"slices.html\">Slices</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"pointers.html\">Pointers</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"optionals.html\">Optionals</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"structs.html\">Structs</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"tuples.html\">Tuples</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"enums.html\">Enums</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"unions.html\">Unions</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"tagged-unions.html\">Tagged Unions</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Standard Library</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"allocators.html\">Allocators</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"arraylist.html\">ArrayList</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"autohashmap.html\">AutoHashMap</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"stringhashmap.html\">StringHashMap</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"hashmap.html\">HashMap</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"sorting.html\">Sorting</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"random.html\">Random</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Command-line Programs</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"arguments.html\">Arguments</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"environment-variables.html\">Environment Variables</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"exit-status.html\">Exit Status</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Async/Await and I/O</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"async.html\">Async</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"io-implementations.html\">Io Implementations</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"queue.html\">Queue</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"file-system.html\">File System</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"text-io.html\">Text I/O</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"binary-io.html\">Binary I/O</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Comptime</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"comptime.html\">Comptime</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"precomputed-data.html\">Precomputed Data</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"generic-functions.html\">Generic Functions</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"generic-types.html\">Generic Types</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"reflection.html\">Reflection</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Zig Tooling</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"build-system.html\">Build System</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Zig and C</h2>\n<ul>\n\n<li><a href=\"using-c.html\">Using C</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"c-types.html\">C Types</a></li>\n\n<li><a href=\"time-and-date.html\">Time and Date</a></li>\n\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>\n\t<a href=\"index.html\">Zig by Example</a>\n\t·\n\t<a href=\"about.html\">about</a>\n\t·\n\t<a href=\"https://codeberg.org/levin/zigbyexample\">source</a>\n</p>\n\n</div></DIV>","content_text":"Zig is a general-purpose programming language and toolchain for maintaining robust, optimal and reusable software. Please read the official documentation to learn more. Zig by Example is a hands-on introduction to Zig using annotated example programs. The examples are written for version 0.16. Check which version you’re using if something isn’t working. Getting Started Hello, World! Formatted Output Unit Tests Basic Types Variables Illegal Behavior Build Modes Basic Types Integers Integer Operators Floating-point Numbers Functions and Errors Functions Errors Assertions Control Flow If Statements Switch Statements While Loops For Loops Blocks Defer Errdefer Compound Types Arrays Slices Pointers Optionals Structs Tuples Enums Unions Tagged Unions Standard Library Allocators ArrayList AutoHashMap StringHashMap HashMap Sorting Random Command-line Programs Arguments Environment Variables Exit Status Async/Await and I/O Async Io Implementations Queue File System Text I/O Binary I/O Comptime Comptime Precomputed Data Generic Functions Generic Types Reflection Zig Tooling Build System Zig and C Using C C Types Time and Date Zig by Example · about · source","fetched_at":"2026-07-26T12:28:55.770Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p>\n<a href=\"https://ziglang.org/\">Zig</a> is a general-purpose programming language and toolchain for maintaining robust, optimal and